# HTTP client — the other half of the M2 validation project (docs/10-roadmap.md,
# M2 gate: "a small HTTP client+server project passes validation").
#
# One GET to http_server.lagom's port (8093), then reads the response until
# the server closes the connection (EOF), and prints it. Networking fails as
# errors (13.1/S-10), so every operation rides `attempt`. These two files are
# skipped by the differential corpus sweep (they need a coordinated peer
# process); crates/lagom_driver/tests/net_validation.rs runs them on both
# backends and across backends.

attempt open connection at 8093 to "localhost" if it fails then
    say problem
otherwise
    make connection equal to result
    attempt put "GET /hello HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: localhost\r\n\r\n" at connection if it fails then
        say problem
    otherwise
        make sent equal to result
    make changing answer equal to ""
    make changing reached end equal to false
    repeat while reached end is equal to false
        attempt take from connection if it fails then
            set reached end to true
        otherwise
            make joined equal to "{answer}{result}"
            set answer to joined
    close connection
    say answer
